R"VG(
# prehistoric7.vg (H-04's second pass): the moon's turns (a calendar on a bone, in the people's marks) and the years' events at
# the turn they fell in (`@event ... pre.cal`); what the years did to a painted wall or a cut stone (the hunts', the pictures').

@root pre.cal.*

# ---- the moon's turns: a calendar on a bone --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.moon (words=23..112)
  {moon.head} {moon.line} {moon.line} {moon.line} {moon.end}
  {moon.head} {moon.line} {moon.line} {moon.end}
  (2) {moon.head} {moon.line} {@event beasts,storm,flood,drought,winter,omen,fair,games,fire,wonder,pest,sickness,famine pre.cal 2} {moon.line} {moon.end}

moon.head (formula)
  (moons>0) A {pre.bone} with notches in a long row, each a night.
  (moons>0) The turns of {moon}, cut on a {pre.bone}.
  (moons=0) A {pre.bone} with notches in a long row, each a day.
  (moons=0) The count of the days, cut on a {pre.bone}.
  A flat bone, notched along both edges.
  (moons>0) The nights of {moon}, as the {people} counted them.
  The year, as {$home} kept it, in {pre.stroke}.

moon.line
  (once) {moon.mark} where {moon.when}.
  (once) {moon.mark} where {moon.when}.
  (once) {moon.mark} where {moon.when}, and another where {moon.when}.
  (once moons>0) A notch for each night; at every full moon {pre.sign.moon}, at every dark one a gap.
  (once moons>0) {count.moon}
  (once moons>1) Two kinds of circles, large and small: the two moons, counted apart.
  (once moons=0) A notch for each day; a long one where {sun.first} stood highest, {pre.hi.mark}.
  (once) A mark like a {tree.n} where the {tree} came into leaf.
  (once seasons=4) A different mark for each of the four seasons: {pre.four}.
  (once seasons=2) Two kinds of marks: wavy lines for {season.now}, short strokes for {season.next}.
  (once comet=1) Once, a star with a tail, scratched deep and rubbed with {colour.holy}.
  (once aurora=1) Once, a row of hanging lines in {colour.holy}: the lights in the north.
  (once) A gap of many notches where nothing was counted, {pre.gap.why}.
  (once) {colour.holy} rubbed into the notches of {season.now}.
  (once) A mark like a bird where the {bird} came back.
  (once) A deep cut where {festival} falls, the same place each turn, {pre.fest.mark}.
  (once) {count.rain}
  (once) The year is cut into {#number} parts, and the first is marked with a {pre.part.first}.
  (once) Where the turn ends, a small drawing of {feast.custom}: the new year's.

moon.mark (people=5)
  A deep cut
  A mark like a leaf
  A small circle
  A double notch
  A mark like a flame
  A cross
  A notch filled with {colour.holy}
  A mark like a fish
  A tiny {herd.sign}
  A spiral
  A tiny hand
  A bar across the notches

moon.when (people=7)
  the {herd} were taken up to the hills
  the river rose
  the first frost came
  the {game} came back
  the {crop2} was ready
  {festival} falls
  the days were longest
  the band moved camp
  the {bird} left
  (desert=0) the {fish} ran
  the {fruit} were ripe
  the {tree} dropped their leaves
  {sun.first} stood lowest
  the young of the {herd} were born
  (desert=1) the dust began
  (desert=1) the cool nights came
  (cold=1) the ice broke
  (coast=1) the sea grew rough

moon.end
  (3) {obj.state}
  The last {pre.stroke.one} is half cut, {pre.lastcut}.
  It ends where the {pre.bone.or} ends, at a {pre.stroke.one} rubbed with {colour.holy}; the count may have gone on elsewhere.
  The turns go round {#number|time} and stop at a {pre.stroke.one} ringed in {colour.holy}.
pre.lastcut
  as if the cutter was called away
  and the {colour.holy} in it is fresher than the rest
  and a hand is pressed beside it
  and {motif.over} are scratched after it
pre.hi.mark
  and a {colour.holy} one where it stood lowest
  and a {bird.one} drawn beside it
  and {motif.over} round it
pre.four (people=1)
  a leaf, a sun, a falling leaf, a flake
  a bud, a {bird.one}, a {tree.n}'s leaf, a flake
  a {herd.sign}, a sun, a {fruit.one}, a closed hand
  a seed, a flame, a basket, a bare {tree.n}
fruit.one
  fruit
  berry
  seed head
pre.gap.why
  the {game} time, when nobody was home
  with {colour.holy} smeared over it
  the ship cannot say why
  in the middle of {season.now}
  where the {herd} were away on the high ground
pre.fest.mark
  filled with {colour.holy}
  with {feast.custom} drawn small beside it
  with {motif.over} round it
  and a hand pressed beside it
pre.part.first
  {bird.one}
  {tree.n}
  fish
  {herd.sign}
  flame
  spiral

# the years' events on the calendar (`@event ... pre.cal`): a mark at the turn where it fell
pre.cal.beasts
  {moon.mark} at the turn where the {game} {pre.cal.came}.
pre.cal.came
  ($e.what=late) came late
  ($e.what=early) came early
  ($e.what=none) should have come, and a gap after it
  ($e.what=many) came in their thousands
  ($e.what=great) came, and the great one was taken
  ($e.what=killed) came, and one of ours was killed
pre.cal.storm
  {moon.mark} at the turn of the {pre.cal.storm.what}, and the notches after it smaller.
pre.cal.storm.what
  ($e.what=wind) great wind
  ($e.what=hail) hail
  ($e.what=snow) deep snow
  ($e.what=dust) dust
  ($e.what=sea) high sea
  ($e.what=lightning) fire from the sky
  ($e.what=rain) long rain
pre.cal.flood
  {moon.mark} where the water came over {$e.place}, and a wavy line under the next {n} notches.
pre.cal.drought
  The notches of {season.now} cut with no mark between them: the dry turn, {#$e.value|year} of them.
pre.cal.winter
  The notches of the winter run on past their place: the winter that did not end.
pre.cal.omen
  ($e.omen=comet) A star with a tail at one turn: the hairy star.
  ($e.omen!=comet) A black circle at one turn: the sign in the sky, {pre.e.when}.
pre.cal.fair
  A ring of hands at one turn: the gathering at {$e.place}.
pre.cal.games
  Figures running at one turn: the games at {$e.place}.
pre.cal.fire
  A flame at one turn, and the next notches sooty: the fire at {$e.place}.
pre.cal.wonder
  {moon.mark} where something was seen at {$e.place}; the ship cannot say what.
pre.cal.pest
  Small dots over one turn: the {pest}, the year they came.
pre.cal.sickness
  Red dots on {n} notches together: the sickness, {pre.e.when}.
pre.cal.famine
  A turn left empty but for {pre.sign.hunger}: the hungry turn.
pre.cal.none
  {moon.mark} where {moon.when}.
# ---- what the years did to a wall, a stone ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wall.state
  {wall.part} {wall.how}.
  {wall.part} {wall.how}, and {wall.how2}.
wall.part
  The {colour.holy}
  The {colour.holy} of the {game}
  The black of the outlines
  The figures on the left
  The lower part, where the {game} are,
  The paint of the {pre.weapon}
  The {game.one}'s head
  The top of the wall
  (accent!=ochre) The ochre under the {colour.holy}
wall.how
  is still good where the rock overhangs
  is gone where the water ran down
  was mixed with fat, and still shines a little in the light
  has been painted over many times
  is flaking at the edges
  was blown on through a reed, not brushed
  was redone later by a less sure hand
  is cracked like dry mud
  is under a skin of lime that the ship looks through
  is darker where a fire burned below it for years
wall.how2
  the rest is faint
  the soot of old fires lies over it
  the ship has filled in what it could
  a crack runs through it
  water still runs down it in {season.now}
  the rock has flaked away below it
stone.state
  {stone.part} {stone.how}.
  {stone.part} {stone.how}, and {stone.how2}.
stone.part
  The cutting
  The {colour.holy} in the lines
  The left side, where the {game} are,
  The lowest part
  The edge of the stone
  The deepest line
  The {game.one} on the right
stone.how
  is worn almost flat by the rain
  is covered with lichen
  is still sharp where the rock leans over it
  was cut again later, deeper
  is split by frost
  is polished where hands rested on it
  is half buried
stone.how2
  the rest is faint
  the ship has filled in what it could
  a crack runs through it
  moss has grown into the north side
)VG"
